WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:16.563
Izzie looked out the window.

2
00:00:16.564 --> 00:00:19.780
It looked cold and gray outside.

3
00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:22.447
But there was no snow.

4
00:00:22.448 --> 00:00:25.384
Christmas was only two weeks away.

5
00:00:25.385 --> 00:00:28.763
Izzie hoped it would be a white Christmas.

6
00:00:28.764 --> 00:00:34.506
She closed her eyes and wished for snow.

7
00:00:34.507 --> 00:00:37.201
"Hey, Izzie," Nina said.

8
00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:41.826
She pointed to a pile of paper plates and paints on the table.

9
00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:45.329
"I think we're doing a craft."

10
00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:48.264
"Oh good," said Izzie.

11
00:00:48.265 --> 00:00:50.605
She loved crafts.

12
00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:55.343
And Miss Shelly always had fun ideas.

13
00:00:55.344 --> 00:00:59.348
"Today we are going to make holiday wreaths."

14
00:00:59.349 --> 00:01:03.610
Miss Shelly held up a glittering gold and silver wreath.

15
00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:07.539
"Ooh, it's pretty," Izzie said.

16
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.148
"I like the angel."

17
00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:13.340
"Me too," Nina said.

18
00:01:13.341 --> 00:01:17.254
"Is that a paper plate?" Jason asked.

19
00:01:17.255 --> 00:01:25.134
"It is. We're going to make wreaths out of paper plates, paint, glue, and some other things."

20
00:01:25.135 --> 00:01:27.691
Miss Shelly held up a bag.

21
00:01:27.692 --> 00:01:31.350
"I have a bunch of old holiday decorations.

22
00:01:31.351 --> 00:01:34.219
You can use whatever you want.

23
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:38.125
First fold your paper plate in half.

24
00:01:38.126 --> 00:01:44.035
And then cut a half circle out of the middle," Miss Shelly said.

25
00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:46.080
"It looks like a wreath already,"

26
00:01:46.081 --> 00:01:49.807
Izzie said, unfolding her plate.

27
00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:54.592
"Now paint your wreath and decorate it with anything you want."

28
00:01:54.593 --> 00:02:00.985
Miss Shelly pointed to a pile of decorations on the table.

29
00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.089
"I'll use this."

30
00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.088
Bobby held up a paper bell.

31
00:02:06.089 --> 00:02:08.539
"And I'll use this."

32
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:14.548
Jason held up a paper menorah.

33
00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:19.849
"Oh!" Nina and Izzie spotted the angel at the same time.

34
00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:24.913
"It's mine!" They both reached for the angel.

35
00:02:24.914 --> 00:02:29.567
"Nina, I really want it," Izzie said.

36
00:02:29.568 --> 00:02:34.875
"So do I, Izzie," Nina said.

37
00:02:34.876 --> 00:02:39.526
"Girls, is there a problem?" Miss Shelly asked.

38
00:02:39.527 --> 00:02:44.465
"Nina wants to use my angel," Izzie said.

39
00:02:44.466 --> 00:02:49.690
"Your angel?" Nina raised her eyebrows.

40
00:02:49.691 --> 00:02:51.274
"Should we share it?"

41
00:02:51.275 --> 00:02:54.713
Nina asked, looking at Miss Shelly.

42
00:02:54.714 --> 00:02:57.139
"You two girls are smart.

43
00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:01.402
I'm sure you'll figure something out," Miss Shelly said.

44
00:03:01.403 --> 00:03:04.836
"Share it?" Izzie repeated.

45
00:03:04.837 --> 00:03:08.184
"How do you share an angel?"

46
00:03:08.185 --> 00:03:12.964
"I guess we could cut it in half," Nina said.

47
00:03:12.965 --> 00:03:15.263
Izzie felt like crying.

48
00:03:15.264 --> 00:03:18.219
She didn't want half of the angel.

49
00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:21.468
Half of the angel would not be beautiful.

50
00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.366
She wanted the whole angel.

51
00:03:25.367 --> 00:03:28.752
"It's okay," Izzie said quietly.

52
00:03:28.753 --> 00:03:31.246
"Nina can have it."

53
00:03:31.247 --> 00:03:34.743
She looked away as Nina took the ornament.

54
00:03:34.744 --> 00:03:37.935
"Thank you, Izzie," Miss Shelly said.

55
00:03:37.936 --> 00:03:43.680
"That was very grown-up."

56
00:03:43.681 --> 00:03:47.190
Izzie saw Nina's wreath drying on the floor.

57
00:03:47.191 --> 00:03:49.663
It looked good.

58
00:03:49.664 --> 00:03:53.967
"Please make it snow," Izzie whispered to the angel.

59
00:03:53.968 --> 00:04:00.346
While their wreaths were drying, Miss Shelly brought out a bucket of jingle bells.

60
00:04:00.347 --> 00:04:06.057
They sang holiday songs and shook their bells.

61
00:04:06.058 --> 00:04:12.070
Before Izzie knew it, it was time to go home.

62
00:04:12.071 --> 00:04:16.807
"What a cute wreath, Izzie!" Izzie's mom exclaimed.

63
00:04:16.808 --> 00:04:21.118
She and Nina's mom were holding up the wreaths.

64
00:04:21.119 --> 00:04:25.941
"Izzie, come look!" Nina suddenly shouted.

65
00:04:25.942 --> 00:04:29.187
Izzie ran to the window.

66
00:04:29.188 --> 00:04:31.035
She couldn't believe it.

67
00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.065
It was snowing!

68
00:04:33.066 --> 00:04:35.623
Her wish had come true.

69
00:04:35.624 --> 00:04:39.746
She looked at Nina's wreath and silently thanked the angel.

70
00:04:39.747 --> 00:04:42.549
Then she turned to Nina.

71
00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:50.399
"Come on, let's catch snowflakes!"
